---
description: Media uploads — MIME/size validation, SVG sanitization, no executable types
globs: **/app/**/*Media*.php,**/app/**/*Upload*.php,**/config/media.php
alwaysApply: false
---

# Upload security

- Validate size and MIME (extension **and** detected type) before storing, through one shared request or service method — never `addMedia($file)` straight from a controller.
- Sanitize every `image/svg+xml` upload with an allowlist-based SVG sanitizer (elements and attributes) before writing it. Reject the file if sanitizing fails. As a backstop, also reject output that still contains `<script`, `on*=` handlers, `javascript:`, or `foreignObject`.
- Never allow executable types (HTML, PHP, JS) in the media config.
- Files that are rendered inline as SVG (icons) must be SVG-only and sanitized; raster images render through `<img>`.
- Heavy post-processing (WebP, thumbnails) is queued (`laravel/queues.mdc`).
- Don't change the public URL shape of stored files without a dedicated migration.

```php
// BAD
$model->addMedia($file)->toMediaCollection('hero');

// GOOD
$this->mediaService->prepareUploadedFile($file);   // validate + sanitize
$media = $model->addMedia($file)->toMediaCollection($collection);
$this->mediaService->queueOrFinalize($media);
```
